        <div id="powering-it" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Battery Operated AC: Runtime and Power Math
          </h2>

          <p>
            Every real battery operated AC comes down to one division: usable watt-hours divided by average watts. Lithium batteries give you roughly 85% of their rated capacity once inverter and conversion losses are counted. A 1,024Wh battery therefore gives about 870Wh. At a 300 watt average that is just under three hours; at 150 watts on an eco setting in a cool evening, closer to six. Manufacturer runtime claims of eight hours assume the gentle end of that range.
          </p>

          <p>
            The average draw is what you control. A compressor works hardest in the first 20 to 30 minutes while it pulls the cabin down, then cycles or slows. Pre-cooling the car on wall or shore power before you unplug, closing the windows, covering the glass and setting a modest target such as 75 degrees instead of 65 can halve the average draw. Running a unit on maximum in a sunny car is the fastest way to turn a 1kWh battery into a two-hour battery.
          </p>

          <p>
            Most people end up powering these units from a portable power station rather than a dedicated add-on battery, because the station also runs a fridge, lights and phones. Our <a href="/best-portable-power-station-for-camping/">camping power station rankings</a> cover the units that pair best with car AC, and <a href="/can-a-portable-power-station-run-an-air-conditioner/">can a portable power station run an air conditioner</a> walks through the same math for larger window and RV units. If you are not sure how big a battery you need, <a href="/what-size-portable-power-station-do-i-need/">our power station sizing guide</a> has a worksheet.
          </p>

          <p>
            Pick LiFePO4 where you can. A car interior gets hot even when the AC is off, and heat ages lithium batteries. LiFePO4 packs, like the WAVE 3 add-on battery and most current EcoFlow, Jackery, Anker and Bluetti stations, tolerate heat better and are rated for thousands of cycles rather than hundreds. Our <a href="/lifepo4-vs-lithium-ion-power-stations/">LiFePO4 vs lithium-ion explainer</a> covers the chemistry in more detail.
          </p>

